course: dictionary
lesson: 3163
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. The word emote is a good example. As a verb, to emote means to show feelings in a strong, often over-the-top way, especially when acting. An actor who emotes too much is overacting.
explain: In games, emote is a noun. An emote is a small animation or picture that a character does to show a feeling, like a dance or a wave. Read this: «By nine o'clock that evening he had spent all three — a skin, a glider, an emote of a dancing hot dog». The skin and the glider are things you buy in a game, so the emote is a game item too.
explain: Ask yourself: is this about a play, or about a game? Is someone showing a feeling, or is it a dance? Then swap in your meaning. Trying "a strong feeling of a dancing hot dog" does not make sense, so here emote must mean the game animation.
fact: Emote can be a verb (to emote, he emotes, he emoted, emoting) or a noun (an emote, emotes).
fact: As a verb, «emote» means to show feelings strongly, often too much, especially when acting.
fact: As a noun in gaming, «emote» means a small animation or picture showing a feeling, like a dance or a wave.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «emote on stage», «buy an emote» and «use an emote».
fact: One word can have two meanings, so always check the context to find the right one.
exercise: An actor who emotes too much on stage is doing what? | *Overacting | Sleeping through the play | Singing in tune | Forgetting every line
exercise: «He spent all his money on a skin, a glider and an emote of a dancing hot dog.» What is the emote in this sentence? | A feeling he showed to his friends | *A dance animation a character does in a game | A hot dog sold at a football match | A kind of games console
exercise: Which phrase uses emote as a noun? | *Buy an emote | Emote on stage | To emote is hard | Emoting in the rain
test: A drama teacher says, «Don't emote so much, just speak your lines.» What does she mean? | Learn the lines faster | Sing louder | Stand still in the light | *Show too many feelings, over the top
test: A child says, «I used an emote to wave at my friend in the game.» What is an emote here? | *A small animation that shows a feeling, like a wave | A slow walk in the park | A kind of games console | A dance of a sad frog
exam: Read this: «Ravi emoted so much at the audition that the judges laughed, but he got the part.» What does emoted mean here? | Copied a game character's dance | Forgot all the words | *Showed feelings strongly and over the top | Ran off the stage
